WEBVTT

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.860
RALPH: You know what
I just realized?

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.620
The sun never rises
or sets here...

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.380
because everything's
always on.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.340
Well, now, isn't that
an astute observation?

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.500
I know, right?

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:17.780
You know,
other than KnowsMore,

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.660
I'm probably the smartest guy
on the Internet.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.500
(LAUGHS) Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.700
Yo, V. We're about to come
back online. You ready?

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.140
Be right there!

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.580
Hey, Ralph,
don't be a stranger!

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:30.860
Well, I can't be much stranger
than you, Shank.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.980
Oh. That's a good dad joke.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.620
Hey, don't forget.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:38.620
You know Shank added my code
and everything,

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.340
so I'll be able to regenerate.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:41.700
I'm gonna be totally safe.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:44.140
No, I know.
It's gonna be great.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.740
You found your dream game.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.380
Yeah, I did.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.060
I did.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.020
So, uh...

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:55.020
I guess I should probably
head in there now, you know?

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.300
Oh, before you go,
I wanted to give you this.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:01.820
Oh, I'm so sorry
I broke it, Ralph.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.660
No, no. It's okay.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:06.260
Now we can both
have a half. See?

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:07.740
(CHUCKLES)

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:09.140
Yeah!

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.660
I love you so much.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.340
I'm really gonna miss you.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.940
I'm gonna miss you too, kid.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:27.700
I really am.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:34.500
All right.

00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:38.140
Okay, getting a little clingy
on me, here.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:42.700
Go on. Get out of here.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.540
The world's
waiting for you, kid.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.740
RALPH: (SIGHS) I'll be honest,

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:46.140
it still feels kind of weird
around here.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.180
I mean, a lot has changed.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:49.740
Even though we got
that steering wheel

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:50.820
and saved Sugar Rush...

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.060
it's never really gonna
be the same.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:56.220
For one thing,
the racers aren't even

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.500
that obnoxious anymore.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.140
Oh, golly. I'm sorry
you didn't win, Taffyta.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.620
Pfft! Our friendship
is much more important to me

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.060
than winning, Rancis.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:05.580
Losing builds character!

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.700
Everyone's a winner, Taffyta.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:10.500
RALPH: Felix and Calhoun,
as goofy as they are,

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.620
they turned out to be
pretty great parents.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.260
I gotta hand it to you two,

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.700
how on earth
did you tame those things?

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.060
It's simple, Surge.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:20.540
The key to parenting is...

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.500
-(CARS WHOOSHING)
-(FELIX TALKING INDISTINCTLY)

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.500
And then what you do is...

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:26.580
(CARS WHOOSHING)

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.140
(CALHOUN TALKING INDISTINCTLY)

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:31.340
And that is the secret
to raising perfect children.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:34.740
Wow, I wish every parent
could hear that.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.220
RALPH: I'm keeping busy, too.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.020
I finally joined
Zangief's book club.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.140
Good point, Bison.
And how about you, Ralph?

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:42.140
Do you feel Dostoyevsky

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:44.540
intended to make
narrator unreliable?

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.220
Um... (EXHALES)

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.340
(STAMMERS) I do and I don't.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.860
You do, and you don't.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:53.460
Duality.
That's really deep, Ralph.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:54.780
Thanks, Sonic.

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:57.300
(WHISPERING) I don't know
what I'm talking about.

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:59.860
Oh. And we got this new thing
we do every Friday night...

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:02.140
where we all go and hang out
in a different game.

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.820
I actually hosted this week.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:05.020
Heyo!

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:07.620
Hope you're all hungry.
I made burnt pie.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:09.500
What's burnt pie, Wreck-It?

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:11.980
Oh, it's just a pie
that you burn.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:13.180
You can use any pie.

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:14.580
You just leave it in the oven
too long.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:16.060
(COUGHS, CLEARS THROAT)

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:20.260
Yeah, we really do
have a lot of fun.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:24.060
I guess that's pretty much
all the news I got for you.

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.860
Oh, man, your stories
never disappoint, Ralph.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:28.660
I just wish
we could hang out sooner.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:30.180
Yeah. Me, too.

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:31.660
When did you say you were
getting those days off?

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:34.540
Uh, our upgrade
starts on January 25th,

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.180
so, like, two months from now.

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:38.860
Oh, that'll go by in a flash.
Oh, speaking of which...

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.220
you want me to bring you
anything from home

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.300
when I come visit?

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.300
Oh! You know what
I cannot find

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:44.980
anywhere on the Internet?

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:47.740
A halfway decent
BurgerTime burger.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:50.020
I've been talking them up
to Shank and the crew.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:52.020
And honestly, I think
they're starting to think

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.100
I'm making it up.

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:54.500
All right, consider it done.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:56.220
I'll bring you guys
a truckload.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.740
Well, sun's coming up already.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.220
Guess I better get to it.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:03.580
Yeah, me too.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:04.660
Talk next week?

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:06.540
I shall await your call,
madam.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:11.420
Then, adieu, adieu,
farting is such sweet sorrow.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:13.780
-(CHUCKLES)
-So long, stinkbrain.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.460
Bye, kid.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:17.900
(BEEPS)

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.340
(SIGHS)

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:31.820
Hey.
You doing okay there, Ralph?

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:36.300
Yeah, I am, actually.
I'm doing great.

00:05:36.460 --> 00:05:39.140
Come on, Felix.
Let's get to work, buddy.

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:56.900
(UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING)

